water-data

# Emacs lock files -- symlinks to "user@host:pid", committed once by a stray `git add -A`
.#*

# The excerpt store. A few pages cut out of a document's PDF and published
# beside it, so an item resting on one letter can link to that letter rather
# than to a 200-page packet. There are 622 of them and they weigh 483 MB --
# 63% of a deploy artifact that had reached 767 MB against GitHub Pages' 1 GB
# ceiling, which is where it started timing out: the deploy job spent ten
# minutes in `syncing_files` and then aborted, twice. So the files live in
# Google Cloud Storage now and the bucket is the only copy --
# `Router.excerpt` points straight at it. See infra/ for the bucket and
# `npm run excerpts:upload` for how one gets there.
#
# Gitignored rather than merely moved out of `static/`, so the repository
# stops growing by ~50 MB a Council packet. The bucket keeps every version of
# every object, which is what stands in for the history git is no longer
# keeping. `npm run excerpts:download` fetches the corpus into a fresh
# checkout.
/excerpts/

# OpenTofu's working directory and state. State names the bucket and its
# generation numbers rather than any secret, but it is machine-written and
# belongs to whoever applied it, not to the repository.
#
# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT here: it pins the provider
# versions an apply resolved, the same job package-lock.json does, so it is
# committed and everyone applies against the same provider.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
/infra/terraform.tfvars
